Subject: server: automatic slot KV persistence + read-only-dir resilience

With --slot-save-path set, restore autosave-slot-<id>.bin into each slot at startup and rewrite them on graceful shutdown (SIGINT/SIGTERM), so prompt KV survives restarts without /slots API calls. --no-slot-autosave opts out. Failures (missing/stale/corrupt file, unwritable dir) warn and degrade to a cold start.
An unwritable --slot-save-path (e.g. baked-in relative path with a read-only CWD) previously aborted startup during arg parsing; it now falls back to ~/.cache/llamafile/kv, then to disabled, never fatal.
Known gaps: slots already migrated to the in-RAM prompt cache (cache_idle_slots) have no tokens to autosave; media slot states still cannot serialize; the MTP drafter context is not restored (first verify rounds after restart draft at reduced acceptance until re-warmed).


